mmposttrainbench
================

This project is a multimodal fork of PostTrainBench.

Derived work:
  PostTrainBench — https://github.com/aisa-group/PostTrainBench
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025 Ben Rank, Hardik Bhatnagar,
  Matthias Bethge, Maksym Andriushchenko
  (see LICENSE — retained verbatim as required by the MIT License).

mmposttrainbench extends PostTrainBench from text-LLM post-training to
multimodal (audio / image / video) post-training of Qwen3-Omni-30B-A3B across
8 benchmarks (mmau, mmar, mmmu_pro, video_mmmu, videomme_v2, jointavbench,
omnivideobench, mmswe), and replaces the HTCondor + apptainer run path with a
Docker separate-verifier pipeline (runs on any GPU host; scheduler-agnostic).

Multimodal extensions, the Docker orchestration (src/docker/), the omni eval
stack (eval_omni/, src/eval/ multimodal adapters), and the harbor build-context
adapter (src/harbor_adapter/) are:
  Copyright (c) 2025 mmposttrainbench maintainers
  Licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE).

Benchmark datasets are the property of their respective authors and are
downloaded from their public HuggingFace repositories at prepare time
(see src/docker/resources.json); they are not redistributed by this repository.
